"Rak Thai Kitchen Menu (Latest Full Update 2026) (https://rak-thai-kitchen.hey-restaurants.com/menu)\nciteturn759search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/plain; \nRak Thai Kitchen Menu (Latest Full Update 2026) Rak Thai Kitchen Menu Menu and portfolio Stir-Fried Dishes Mongolian Stir-fried with homemade Mongolian sauce and vegetables. A$21.50 Sweet And Sour With your choice of meat. Stir-fried with homemade sweet and sour sauce, pineapple, tomatoes, cucumber and vegetables. A$18.50 Chili Fish Spicy. Deep-fried fish fillets cooked with homemade sweet chili sauce. A$24.00 Spicy Spicy. With your choice of meat. Stir-fried with curry paste, coconut cream, green peppercorn and vegetables. A$20.50 Black Bean Stir-fried with homemade black bean sauce and vegetables. A$20.50 Basil Spicy. With your choice of meat. Stir-fried with fresh basil, homemade chili paste and vegetables. A$20.50 Cashew Nut Spicy. Stir-fried with homemade chili paste and vegetables topped with roasted cashew nut. A$21.50 Garlic And Pepper Stir-fried with garlic, pepper and vegetables. A$20.50 Peanut Sauce Steamed meat and vegetables topped with homemade peanut sauce. A$20.50 Oyster Sauce Stir-fried with oyster sauce and vegetables. A$18.50 Chili Duck Spicy. Stir-fried roasted duck with homemade chili paste and vegetables. A$25.50 Ginger With your choice of meat. Stir-fried with ginger, vegetables and white wine. A$18.50 Rice Bowl Pad Kra Prao Rice Bowl Stir fried basil minced pork served with rice and fried egg A$24.00 Salad Seafood Salad Spicy. Mixed seafood cooked with chili, lime juice and Thai herbs. A$25.50 Beef Salad Spicy. Grilled beef cooked with chili, lime juice and Thai herbs. A$23.50 Larb Spicy. Chopped meat cooked with Thai herbs, chili powder, lime juice and mint leaves. A$23.00 Rice and Noodles Tom Yum Prawn Noodle Soup Spicy. Thin rice noodle in tom yum prawn soup. A$23.50 Mongolian Noodle Stir-fried ... onions. A$23.00 Green Curry (Hot) With your choice of meat. Simmered with green curry paste in coconut milk, bamboo shoots and vegetables. A$21.50 Choo Chee Curry (Medium Hot) Simmered with choo chee curry paste in creamy coconut cream and vegetables. A$24.00 Massaman Beef Curry (Mild) Stewed beef simmered in coconut milk, mix Thai herbs, potatoes and onions. A$24.00 Panang Curry... boneless chicken or pork topped with homemade plum sauce. A$22.50 Rak Thai Kitchen’s menu feels like a confident showcase of classic Thai comfort dishes with bold, familiar flavors. The stir-fried selection stands out first, especially the Mongolian style dishes that balance savory sauce with tender meat, while the Sweet and Sour options deliver a clean, glossy tang without overpowering the ingredients. Chili Fish brings a sharper kick, ideal for those who enjoy a bit of heat with depth. The Pad Kra Prao Rice Bowl is a reliable highlight, fragrant with basil and chili, simple but deeply satisfying. For lighter choices, the salads offer contrast: the Seafood Salad is fresh and zesty, the Beef Salad has a satisfying richness, and Larb delivers that signature Thai balance of herbs, citrus, and spice. Noodle lovers are well covered. Tom Yum Prawn Noodle Soup combines aromatic broth with bright acidity, while Pad Thai Noodle stays true to its crowd-pleasing roots. Curries are clearly defined by heat level, from the mild Yellow Chicken Curry to the fiery Green Curry, each creamy and well-spiced. Entrées like Satay and Fried Wonton are crisp and comforting, and the crispy dishes paired with honey, tamarind, or sweet and sour sauce round out the menu with indulgent textures and flavors. Discover Rak Thai Kitchen menu with the latest update. Explore dishes, seasonal highlights, and customer favorites for every taste in 2026.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSport Fair (https://shopping.saigoncentre.com.vn/en/store-directory/sport-fair)\nciteturn759search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content ty